Z||000000||fierose||07-07-2000||01:51 AM||||I (85SE) was just wondering if you guys could help me out.  I have this clicking sound coming from my engine.  Upon further examination using my dowel rod it seems like the sound is coming from the fuel return line coming out of my throttle body.  You can hear the sound at the fuel feed where the fuel filter is located but it's not as strong.  Everywhere else in the engine bay I listened for the sound I couldn't really hear it.  I'm wondering if your fuel pump might make this sound on it's last leg, I did run my tank dry a few times when I first got the car 12 months ago. I then realized 1/4 tank meant go get gas.  Or maybe something in the TBI that could make this sound?  I looked in to checking my fuel pressure but the fitting and gages for TBI were like $50.  I was also wondering if a worn fuel pump could cause a loss of performance.  Any suggestions you guys have would be greatly appreciated.  It's an everyday driver so I don't won't to left on the side of the road.  Thanks.  Cliff you tha man!<P>J.D.||||reg||5
